<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949</span> · Also known as CPPCC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference is a political advisory body of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>, bringing together the Communist Party, the minor parties and other groups under the party's leadership. Its first session in September 1949 acted as a constituent assembly, adopting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/common-program">Common Program</a> and electing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> as chairman of the new government, and it still meets each year alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-peoples-congress">National People's Congress</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chinese-peoples-political-consultative-conference.jpg" alt="Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference" width="320" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinese_People%27s_Political_Consultative_Conference_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
